  "openQuestionsResolved": [
    {
      "question": "Does Approval need a REVISION_REQUESTED status or just REJECTED?",
      "decision": "REVISION_REQUESTED retained as a distinct status",
      "rationale": "Already present in Approval model and ApprovalStatus enum; communicates that work must continue before re-submission without permanently closing the deliverable"
    },
    {
      "question": "Auth strategy: JWT vs token auth, and how are WebSocket connections authenticated?",
      "decision": "Dual auth: REST endpoints use dj-rest-auth + DRF TokenAuthentication. WebSocket consumers use Channels AuthMiddlewareStack (session-based). dj-rest-auth sets a session cookie on login alongside returning the token, so both transports are authenticated from the same login action.",
      "rationale": "The browser WebSocket API cannot set custom headers, making the Authorization: Token header unavailable on the WebSocket upgrade request. Channels AuthMiddlewareStack reads the Django session cookie, which the browser sends automatically on the upgrade. Enabling session auth alongside token auth is a one-line settings change requiring no custom middleware. This avoids the security risk of passing tokens in query strings (visible in server logs)."
    },
    {
      "question": "File storage backend selection",
      "decision": "django-storages GoogleCloudStorage; already installed and wired via GS_BUCKET_NAME",
      "rationale": "Already present in STORAGES settings; GCSFileStorageAdapter wraps it at the infrastructure boundary so use cases depend only on GCSFileStoragePort"
    },
    {
      "question": "Redis connection authentication",
      "decision": "Password-only auth via REDIS_URL env var for CHANNEL_LAYERS",
      "rationale": "Matches existing VPS Redis configuration; no TLS client cert required"
    },
    {
      "question": "WebSocket / real-time delivery mechanism",
      "decision": "Django Channels with ProtocolTypeRouter; Daphne ASGI server; channels-redis channel layer",
      "rationale": "Acceptance criterion explicitly requires this stack; CHANNEL_LAYERS config points to REDIS_URL"
    },
    {
      "question": "Where do DRF settings and INSTALLED_APPS entries go?",
      "decision": "Add rest_framework, allauth, dj_rest_auth, corsheaders, channels to INSTALLED_APPS; add REST_FRAMEWORK settings block and CHANNEL_LAYERS block to core/settings.py",
      "rationale": "No DRF or allauth registration exists yet; required before any viewset or auth endpoint works"
    }
  ],
  "implementationNotes": "Domain layer is fully scaffolded - do not recreate model.py, value_objects.py, repositories.py, or events.py. All 12 ORM models exist; migration 0001_initial is applied. Work begins with: (1) application/ layer - one file each for use_cases.py and dtos.py following blog app pattern exactly; (2) infrastructure/ layer - repositories.py with private _model_to_entity() mappers, storage.py with GCSFileStorageAdapter, permissions.py with three permission classes; (3) urls.py and views.py (or api_urls.py + api_views.py) wiring DRF router; (4) services/ directory for notification helpers only (approval/file logic lives in use cases). Register djangorestframework, allauth, dj_rest_auth, channels in INSTALLED_APPS before writing viewsets. Add REST_FRAMEWORK settings block with DEFAULT_AUTHENTICATION_CLASSES = [TokenAuthentication] and DEFAULT_PERMISSION_CLASSES = [IsAuthenticated]. Upgrade core/asgi.py to ProtocolTypeRouter after installing channels and daphne. DI pattern: instantiate use cases in viewset action methods, passing concrete Django repository classes to constructors - no service locator. GCSFileStoragePort output port interface lives in application layer; GCSFileStorageAdapter in infrastructure. ActivityEventRecorder domain service is called from every write use case to maintain the audit trail. Seed script target: 2 orgs, 3 projects (ACTIVE, PENDING_APPROVAL, COMPLETE), milestones and deliverables with at least one approved version, 1 OVERDUE invoice, sample messages and files. WebSocket auth: configure dj-rest-auth to set session cookies on login; wrap the Channels URL router in AuthMiddlewareStack in core/asgi.py so consumers receive scope['user']; REST_FRAMEWORK DEFAULT_AUTHENTICATION_CLASSES must include both TokenAuthentication and SessionAuthentication. Consumers must close unauthenticated connections immediately (scope['user'].is_anonymous check in websocket_connect)."
}